    description: ""  # 900d
    fields:  # 900d
      statement: "'hypergumbo config <X>' should reject (with a helpful 'did you mean ...' hint) when X is not a language analyzer — e.g., when X is a framework-linker name like 'airflow-framework-dispatch-linker' or 'akka-http'."  # 900d
      root_cause: "config dispatches on whatever name the user gives, looking up in the catalog without distinguishing 'language analyzer' from 'framework linker' or 'cross-cutting linker'. Affected names include: airflow-framework-dispatch-linker, akka-http, adonisjs, aiohttp, annotation-convention-linker (and 60+ similar). User gets identically-shaped empty JSON, no error signal that the argument was wrong. Same fail-silent class as INV-furop (sketch --require-section)."  # 900d
